{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/73245-khaibit-bloodline-as-cultist","id":73245,"title":"Khaibit [Bloodline] as cultist","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-16T10:05:27-08:00","id":73245,"title":"Khaibit [Bloodline] as cultist","content":"Im currently working on a chronicle set in the years following WWI in the Middle East. I am wondering how well a cult of vampires would function as cultists? Has anyone tried this? Anything has come up to unbalance the game or story? <br /> <br /> What I have so far:<br /> <br /> The Mummy in question (an NPC) has sought and initiated a group of Khaibit to serve her as cultists. This cult is dedicated to serving the Mummy as assassins and acquisition experts (relic thieves). What would motivate a group of vampires to serve in this function (besides the obvious)?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T14:58:50-08:00","id":77341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JoeB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/73245-khaibit-bloodline-as-cultist#post73245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im currently working on a chronicle set in the years following WWI in the Middle East. I am wondering how well a cult of vampires would function as cultists? Has anyone tried this? Anything has come up to unbalance the game or story?<br /> <br /> What I have so far:<br /> <br /> The Mummy in question (an NPC) has sought and initiated a group of Khaibit to serve her as cultists. This cult is dedicated to serving the Mummy as assassins and acquisition experts (relic thieves). What would motivate a group of vampires to serve in this function (besides the obvious)?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if the Mummy in question has Mortal followers as well, then the Khaibit basically have a ready-made Herd to feed off. Plus they are people that the Khaibit don't need to worry about when it comes the Masquerade. Working for the Mummy pretty much exempts them from a lot of the &quot;mortals must not know&quot; rules. <br /> <br /> If the Khaibit are Crone or Ordo then they have pretty good mystical reasons to hang around.<br /> <br /> Mummy's attract occult forces and junk. For Crone its a good way to get hold of non-Sekhem infused magic items that the Mummy might end up collecting but has no &quot;need&quot; of. Plus if you wanted you could have it so Arisen &quot;blood&quot; (congealed Sekhem) has interesting effects on Cruac rituals. <br /> <br /> For Ordo the Mummy herself is a fascinating research opportunity. Mummy tombs (with their life webs) might make Wyrms Nests or one sort or another, or at least create an interest supernatural resonance that could be harnessed. The Mummy herself is the polar-opposite of a Vampire, active for short periods of time but utterly ALIVE while awake. Yet Arisen are also very like Vampires, undead and everylasting (given the right circumstances). Indeed I imagine they would be fascinated by the Arisen's distinction between Deathless and Lifeless types of undead. <br /> <br /> If the Arisen at the head of the cult is either Snake or Jackel headed then they might have a few religious reasons to hang around. Set was said to have traveled to Duat and obviously one of Set's animals in the Snake. This of course depends on the Khaibit in question buying in their Bloodline mysticism a fair bit. <br /> <br /> Those are just some off the top of my head. I'm sure there are more which would be dependent on the socio-political structure of the area. As Vampires are pretty much always involved with those themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T09:48:20-08:00","id":77698,"title":"","content":"The Set animal is... closer to an aardvark. Snakes are only associated with Set so far as Apep is. Quite literally in the Cult of Seth vampire write up, I'm rather sure that the association with snakes is likely more antagonistic as Sethites and especially the Khaibit are to battle invaders as Seth battled Apep. Jackals are associated with Anubis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T10:00:28-08:00","id":77702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/73245-khaibit-bloodline-as-cultist?p=77698#post77698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Set animal is... closer to an aardvark. Snakes are only associated with Set so far as Apep is. Quite literally in the Cult of Seth vampire write up, I'm rather sure that the association with snakes is likely more antagonistic as Sethites and especially the Khaibit are to battle invaders as Seth battled Apep. Jackals are associated with Anubis.</div> </div> </div> </div>All true. Well aware that the Set animal is a bit weird, think its called a &quot;Typhon Beast&quot; bu t obviously that's a Greek interpretation that sprouted from the association between Set and Typhon due to the co-mingling of Greek and Egyptian culture well after the &quot;high Egypt&quot; time period. <br /> <br /> The reason I was thinking of associating the Jackel headed because they are the Mummy's that have a habit of &quot;seeing&quot; beyond the material aspect of the world (as they are slightly more linked to Duat and ghostly stuff). As such they might have some more common ground with Khaibit, who also have a bit of a &quot;see beyond the pale&quot; thing going on. Spirit warriors and all that. <br /> <br /> Due to the Cult of Seth and frankly a fair bit of pop-cultures association between Snakes and Set, I was thinking that Snake Headed might get along with Khaibit for &quot;symbolic&quot; reasons. However, Snake Headed Mummy's do have a habit of looking into riddles, puzzles, mysteries and odd occurrences a little more. Once again, an occult interested Khaibit could do worse then having a Snake Headed Mummy for a companion/sponsor/boss. <br /> <br /> Considering talk on the Vampire forum is that the Khaibit are one of only two old bloodlines getting a rewrite for Blood and Smoke (Neglu are the other, and I guess Malkovians or at least Malkavia have been mentioned as of the new core). I imagine they are going to get a rewrite focusing on fighting the Strix, but that's a presumption on my part. Machine VI is writing it I think. Hopefully he'll drop some hints over on the Vampire forums soon. I'm wondering if the rewrite will make the Khaibit more or less crossover friendly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T12:57:07-07:00","id":88378,"title":"","content":"Irem Set is a Snake, just like how Irem Re is a Lion rather then the Falcon Ra of Egypt. Irem is slightly different from Egypt it is it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T04:58:38-07:00","id":88774,"title":"","content":"Frankly, I've always liked the idea of the Mekhet being the result of some mortal schlub ROYALLY pissing off the Judges of Duat and getting a supremely nasty curse for his trouble. <br /> <br /> Also: If you're running Mummy, I'd absolutely LOVE to play in the game!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1645-autochthon","name":"Autochthon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T00:50:37-07:00","id":90724,"title":"","content":"I wonder if you could recreate the Children of Osiris as a bloodline that has ties to the times of Irem, being that there's speculation that the earliest Mekhet may have existed during the time of Irem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}